# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("Binding groups and cycles": the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else), ch. 7 as ruled (round 3 ST: a gathered dynamic moves at n+1, an owed tick), ch. 9 (a place's first value is read in its birth tick; an event answer is the next tick's input, owed; round 3 DY), ch. 8 (`<-` builds the child and binds its result, the tuple pattern taking the bundle apart), Type System ch. 2 ("Bundles") and rulings TC and PL (a path is a list of lists, one per widget application; a `for` row's places extend the list at its key; a supplier's answer is a widget applied under the host's key): sem-ch09-host-late-plain-part-taken-above's ticks, the child's place 0 the pair's button over the plain part 7, the bundle's plain part 8; no press of it, so the count stays 0. `@Pair` at the child's 0 numbers its button in its own list (`0/0`). Never run: prismc-s4 refuses the program.
test a_late_plain_part_is_taken_by_a_bundle_giver

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1.[1].0: Ui.Label(text="one")
    2.[0/0].0: Ui.Button(label="b 7")
    2.[2].0: Ui.Label(text="7 wide 8 1: none 0")

